-- title:
--   Completed end ring of blown-up supersingular chart as crossing model
-- statement:
--   Arithmetic data: a prime $q\ge 5$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a prime $\ell\ge 3$ with $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$, a field $L$ of characteristic $0$, an element $\xi\in L$ which is a primitive $(q\ell)$-th root of unity, and the hypothesis `hι` that some ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$.
--
--   Function field: an intermediate field $K$ of $L\subseteq L((t))$ equal (hypothesis `hK`) to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $\mathbb Q$-function field [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ)^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ) M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the $L$-subfield of $L((t))$ generated by the image, under coefficientwise extension of scalars, of the field of $q$-expansions attached to the level $(q\ell)^2M'$ and the subgroup $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb Z/(q\ell)^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell)^\times\bigr)$ of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q\ell$.
--
--   Base ring: a discrete valuation ring $A$ which is a domain, Henselian local, with algebraically closed residue field, equipped with an $L$-algebra structure making $L$ its fraction field, with $q\in\mathfrak m_A$ (hypothesis `hAq`) and $\xi$ in the image of $A$ (hypothesis `hξA`), together with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$. An element $j\in K$, non-zero, whose Laurent expansion is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) of the modular invariant (hypothesis `hj`). A uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A$ (hypothesis `hϖ`: $\mathfrak m_A=(\varpi)$) and a tame parameter $\varpi_t\in A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot(\text{unit})$ (hypothesis `hϖt`).
--
--   Supersingular point: writing $C=$ `chartAlgFin A K j` for the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, a maximal ideal $y$ of $C$ containing $\varpi$ (hypotheses `hy`, `hϖy`), such that (hypothesis `hss`) for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi:C\to\Omega$ with kernel $y$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), i.e. every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-trivial $q$-torsion point.
--
--   The hypothesis `hArig` (a uniform Drinfeld-chart witness, summarised here) asserts: for every point $z$ of the two-chart integral model $X=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) such that the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ under the structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}A$ lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of the finite chart `XFin A K j` mapping to $z$ under `ιFin` at which the same supersingularity condition as in `hss` holds, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring map $\sigma:A\to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W=(\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v\in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f-\bigl(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1\bigr)\in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S=W[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v-fu\bigr)$, satisfying the seven riders spelled out below for the pinned witness.
--
--   Pinned witness: a point $z$ of $X$, the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the image of $\varpi$ (hypothesis `hϖz`) lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ (hypothesis `hz`); a point $y'$ of `XFin A K j` with `ιFin` sending $y'$ to $z$ (hypothesis `hy'`), satisfying the supersingularity condition (hypothesis `hss'`) and with $y'$ corresponding to $y$ (hypothesis `hy'y`); a complete discrete valuation domain $W_1$, a ring map $\sigma_1:A\to W_1$ with $\mathfrak m_{W_1}=(\sigma_1\varpi)$, elements $f_1,u_1,v_1\in W_1[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u_1,v_1$ units and $f_1-(X_0X_1^q-X_0^qX_1)\in(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and a ring isomorphism
--   $$e_1:\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;S=W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(C(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1}))v_1-f_1u_1\bigr).$$
--   Here $\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ denotes the $\mathfrak m$-adic completion of the stalk, `toC` the canonical map $\mathcal O_{X,z}\to\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$, `mkS` the quotient map onto $S$, and `germY` the canonical ring map $C\to\mathcal O_{X,z}$ obtained from $\Gamma\!\operatorname{Spec}$ and the germ at $z$ on the image of the finite chart.
--
--   The hypothesis `hW₁` consists of seven clauses for this witness: (1) $e_1$ carries the image of $a\in A$ in $\widehat{\mathcal O_{X,z}}$ to the class of the constant $C(\sigma_1 a)$; (2) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ and every $\tau\in\operatorname{Aut}_L(K)$ which is a level automorphism attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ in the sense of `IsLevelAutAt` (for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of level $\Gamma_H$ with integral $q$-expansions and $g$ non-zero, all $x\in K$ whose Laurent expansion is the ratio of those $q$-expansions, and all embeddings $\iota:L\to\mathbb C$ with $\iota\xi=\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell))$, the complex $q$-expansion of $\tau x$ times that of $g|_k\,\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma$ equals that of $f|_k\,\mathrm{conjElemN}\,(q\ell)\,\gamma$), the map $\tau$ preserves $C$; (3) if moreover $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, then $\tau$ is the identity on $C/y'$; (4) for $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, every such $\tau$ preserving $C$ and inducing the identity on $C/y'$ is transported by $e_1$ to a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$ fixing all constants, with linear part a matrix $M$ over $W_1$ modulo $(X_0,X_1)^2$, and a scalar $c\in W_1$ with $c^{q+1}\equiv1$, $M\equiv c\gamma$ modulo $\mathfrak m_{W_1}$ entrywise, $c\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(\ell)$, and $c\not\equiv1$ if $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; (5) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each containing the class of $C(\sigma_1\varpi)$, each omitting at least one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, and each containing an element $a_iX_0+b_iX_1+h_i$ with $h_i\in(X_0,X_1)^2$ and integers $a_i,b_i$ with $q\nmid a_1b_2-a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions along $e_1\circ$ `toC`; (6) for a prime $P$ of $S$ containing the class of $C(\sigma_1\varpi)$, omitting one of the classes of $X_0,X_1$, and containing an element $X_0+h$ with $h\in(X_0,X_1)^2$, an element $a\in C$ has $\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,a)$ in the contraction of $P$ along $e_1$ if and only if every Laurent coefficient of $a$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak m_A$; (7) $\,$[`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0\in A$ with the class of $\mathrm{jqNModC}-a_0$ in $y'$, an integer $e_0\ge1$ and $h\in(X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ initial form is non-degenerate in the sense that $\sum_{i\le e_0}\operatorname{coeff}_{(i,e_0-i)}(h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit whenever $a,b\in W_1$ are not both non-units and $a^qb-ab^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, with $e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}(\mathrm{jqNModC}-a_0)))$ equal to the class of $h$.
--
--   Weighted centre and $\varpi_t$-chart: an ideal $J$ of $C$ equal (hypothesis `hJ`) to the infimum, over all $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$ and all level automorphisms $\tau$ attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$, of the pullback along $\tau|_C$ of the contraction along $e_1\circ\mathrm{toC}\circ\mathrm{germY}$ of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi_t)$, $X_0$ and $X_1$. An $A$-subalgebra $B$ of $K$ equal (hypothesis `hB`) to the $C$-algebra generated by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ x\varpi_t=i\}$, viewed over $A$. A valuation subring $W$ of $K$ with $B\subseteq W$ (hypothesis `hBW`), subject to: `hR1`, that $C\subseteq B$ and every $f\in K$ is of the form $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\ne0$; `hR2`, that $A\to B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation and $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that $W\cap L$ is exactly the image of $A$, that $\mathfrak m_W=(\varpi)$, that $W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that $y$ is the contraction of $\mathfrak m_W$ to $C$, and that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ away from $\mathfrak m_W$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for any $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k_A$ of $A$ there is a surjection $\rho:B\to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k_A`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) with kernel the elements lying in $\mathfrak m_W$, compatible with $A\to k_A$, and equivariant for level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $W$, the equivariance being through [`DrinfeldCurve.hAction`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L325) at an element $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,c)$ of `hSubgroup q` with $c\ne1$ when $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)$ and $\tau\ne\mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms attached to $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained as the image of $\mathfrak m_W\cap B$ under some level automorphism with $\gamma\in\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose such translates lie in $\mathfrak m_W$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that level automorphisms with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ preserving $y$ preserve $W$. Further hypotheses `hjK`, `hjC`: [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L (q*ℓ)`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$.
--
--   End data: an integer $m\ge1$ with $\varpi^m=\varpi_t\cdot(\text{unit})$ (hypotheses `hm1`, `hmt`), and a subring $\mathcal O$ of $K$ satisfying the end pin `hO`: there is $a\in J$, non-zero in $K$, such that, with $B_a$ the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ generated over $C$ by $\{x\in K:\exists i\in J,\ xa=i\}$ (the affine blow-up chart), there is a maximal ideal $P$ of $B_a$ with $\mathcal O$ the localisation of $B_a$ at $P$ (an $f\in K$ lies in $\mathcal O$ exactly when $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B_a$, $h\notin P$), such that every element of $y$ lying in $\mathcal O$ is a non-unit of $\mathcal O$, and such that $B$ is not contained in $\mathcal O$.
--
--   Conclusion. First, $\mathcal O\subseteq W$. Second, $\mathcal O$ is local and Noetherian, $C\subseteq\mathcal O$ (witness `hCO`), and:
--
--   (i) for $x\in L$, the image of $x$ in $K$ lies in $\mathcal O$ if and only if $x$ comes from $A$;
--
--   (ii) for every $f\in\mathcal O$ there is $a\in A$ whose image lies in $\mathcal O$ with $f-a$ a non-unit of $\mathcal O$;
--
--   (iii) there is a ring homomorphism $\Lambda:S\to\widehat{\mathcal O}$ into the $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$-adic completion of $\mathcal O$ such that $\Lambda(e_1(\mathrm{toC}(\mathrm{germY}\,c)))$ is the image of $c$ in $\widehat{\mathcal O}$ for every $c\in C$, and such that for every $N$, $\Lambda$ maps the $N$-th power of the ideal of $S$ generated by the classes of $C(\sigma_1\varpi)$, $X_0$, $X_1$ into the $N$-th power of the ideal of $\widehat{\mathcal O}$ generated by the image of $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal O}$;
--
--   (iv) there is a ring isomorphism
--   $$\iota:\widehat{\mathcal O}\;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\;\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,\widehat A\,\bigl(\varpi^m\bigr)=\widehat A[[X_0,X_1]]/\bigl(X_0X_1-C(\varpi^m)\bigr),$$
--   where $\widehat A$ is the $\mathfrak m_A$-adic completion of $A$ and $\varpi^m$ denotes the $m$-th power of the image of $\varpi$, such that $\iota$ carries the image in $\widehat{\mathcal O}$ of any $a\in A$ lying in $\mathcal O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $a$ in $\widehat A$; moreover
--
--   (iv-a) there exist a ring homomorphism $\rho:W_1\to\widehat A$, elements $p_0,p_1\in W_1$ and elements $\alpha,\beta$ of the crossing model such that $\rho\circ\sigma_1$ is the map $A\to\widehat A$, $\rho$ sends non-units to non-units, at least one of $p_0,p_1$ is a unit, $p_0^qp_1-p_0p_1^q\in\mathfrak m_{W_1}$, the elements $\alpha-\mathrm{const}(\rho p_0)$ and $\beta-\mathrm{const}(\rho p_1)$ are non-units, and
--   $$\iota(\Lambda(\overline{X_0}))=V\cdot\alpha,\qquad \iota(\Lambda(\overline{X_1}))=V\cdot\beta,\qquad \iota(\Lambda(\overline{C(w)}))=\mathrm{const}(\rho w)\ \ (w\in W_1),$$
--   where $U$ and $V$ denote the two distinguished coordinate elements `UVCrossingModel.U` and `UVCrossingModel.V` of the crossing model;
--
--   (iv-b) $\varpi$ lies in $\mathcal O$, and there are $c_x,c_y\in\mathcal O$, a unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ and units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of the crossing model with $c_xc_y=\varpi^m u$ in $\mathcal O$, with $\iota$ of the image of $c_x$ equal to $\gamma_U\cdot U$ and $\iota$ of the image of $c_y$ equal to $\gamma_V\cdot V$, with $c_y$ lying in $\mathfrak m_W$ whenever it lies in $W$, and with $c_x$ lying outside $\mathfrak m_W$ whenever it lies in $W$.
--
--   This is the local analysis, in the style of Katz–Mazur's study of the Igusa curve and of the supersingular points of modular curves, at an end of the blow-up of the supersingular chart: the completed local ring at such an end is identified with the crossing model $\widehat A[[U,V]]/(UV-\varpi^m)$, together with the chart map $\Lambda$ from the Drinfeld-chart presentation $S$, an $\mathbb F_q$-rational tangent direction $(p_0:p_1)$, and coordinates $c_x,c_y$ on the two branches. It is the shared input for the construction of a crossing presentation of $j$ at an end, for the trichotomy of exceptional primes, and for the equivariant form of the end isomorphism under level automorphisms.
